course: dictionary
lesson: 13907
title: The word latest
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Latest is a word you will see often, in news, adverts and school notes. It usually means the newest, or the most recent. «Mia bought the latest phone, which came out this week.» The newest phone is the latest one, so latest means most recent.
explain: Latest can also mean the last possible time. «The library closes at five, so the latest you can return a book is five o'clock.» That means not after five. Add «at the latest» and it means no later than that time: «Hand in your homework by Friday at the latest.»
explain: Latest is the last form of the word late: late, later, latest. To find out which meaning is right, ask: does this sentence mean newest, or does it mean the last possible time? Then try your meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Latest means newest or most recent, as in «the latest news».
fact: Latest can also mean the last possible time, as in «the latest you can arrive is noon».
fact: «At the latest» means not later than that time, as in «finish by Friday at the latest».
fact: The latest can be a noun too: «The latest is a new film about dinosaurs» means the newest film.
fact: Latest is the superlative of late, so late, later and latest belong together.
exercise: «She always wants the latest trainers.» What does latest mean here? | *The newest ones, just out in the shops | Lost and found | Very old and worn out | The cheapest ones in the shop
exercise: «The shop closes at six, so the latest you can arrive is quarter to six.» What does latest mean here? | *The last possible time | Very fast | Never at all | The first possible time
exercise: Dad's note says, «Send the form back by Monday at the latest.» Which day is the deadline? | Friday, at the start of the week | Any day next week | Tuesday | *Monday, or earlier
test: «Ben read the latest news on his tablet.» What is the latest news? | Old news from last year | Stories about lunch | Stories from a library book | *The most recent news
test: «You must be home by ten at the latest.» What does at the latest mean here? | Ten minutes after ten | Exactly ten, and not before | Any time at all | *No later than ten
exam: «The latest version of the app has new colours.» What does the latest version mean? | *The newest version | The version with the most mistakes | A version for babies | An old version from years ago
